WEBVTT

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.029
Come in.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:34.200
How are you doing?

00:00:37.328 --> 00:00:39.998
I finally started to grasp...

00:00:39.998 --> 00:00:42.500
Aquarion's melody...

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.003
The ultimate melody that I seek...

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:47.547
I'm almost there.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:49.507
You must not push too hard.

00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:51.468
Shrade, your body is--

00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:52.844
I don't care...

00:00:52.844 --> 00:00:56.348
If I can produce that
melody with my own hands,

00:00:56.348 --> 00:00:59.184
even if my body is consumed by a devil...

00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:06.441
This special authorization will allow
your discharge from the hospital.

00:01:06.441 --> 00:01:11.946
But what you seek goes hand-in-hand
with the constant temptation of death.

00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:15.533
Please try to keep that in mind.

00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:23.958
The sound of life echoes precisely
when it goes hand-in-hand with death.

00:01:26.961 --> 00:01:28.463
<i>Osore!</i>

00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:32.509
<i>Living your life don't give up now</i>
<i>keep moving on</i>

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:38.139
<i>Kimi o dakishimeru</i>
<i>nando mo nando mo nando mo</i>

00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:43.978
<i>Ashita boku wa kimi ni deau darou</i>

00:01:43.978 --> 00:01:49.693
<i>Wazuka na hoshi akari o tayori ni</i>

00:01:49.693 --> 00:01:55.782
<i>Boku ni wa kimi ga wakaru yo wakaru yo</i>

00:01:55.782 --> 00:02:05.709
<i>Sen oku no toki o koe </i>
<i>futari hiraku densetsu no tobira</i>

00:02:05.709 --> 00:02:11.589
<i>Naraku no ao tobikoete</i>

00:02:11.589 --> 00:02:17.387
<i>Kimi to hai ni naru tame</i>

00:02:17.387 --> 00:02:28.314
<i>Nagaki rinne o</i>
<i>kanashimi tsurete tabi shite kitanda</i>

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:31.359
<i>Zenryoku de mikansei</i>

00:02:31.359 --> 00:02:34.237
<i>Kimi no tonari de</i>

00:02:34.237 --> 00:02:40.035
<i>Kawaita kokoro hodoke chi o nagasu kedo</i>

00:02:40.035 --> 00:02:43.079
<i>Soba ni iru yo zutto</i>

00:02:43.079 --> 00:02:45.957
<i>Yorisotte zutto</i>

00:02:45.957 --> 00:02:50.628
<i>Futari hikari no fune ni noru</i>

00:02:50.628 --> 00:02:56.426
<i>Kaze no hajimari no oto kanadeyou (Mezame!)</i>

00:02:59.304 --> 00:03:00.930
"Midnight Girl"

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:03.516
"Midnight Girl"
Everyone! Are you really okay with this?!

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:06.561
It's been already a week
since the Berlin Wall collapsed.

00:03:06.561 --> 00:03:11.066
And yet, there's still an invisible wall
that separates us guys and girls!

00:03:11.066 --> 00:03:13.193
Isn't this the moment to remove the barrier

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:15.987
between guys and girls and expose
our hearts to each other?!

00:03:15.987 --> 00:03:17.947
What's this fuss all about?

00:03:17.947 --> 00:03:21.326
Someone suddenly started a stupid speech.

00:03:21.326 --> 00:03:23.536
Hey, Andy, I think that's enough.

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:24.913
You idiot!

00:03:24.913 --> 00:03:28.708
Guys! I suggest an emergency
change in the seating arrangements!

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.335
Oh, so this fuss was about changing seats?

00:03:30.335 --> 00:03:31.961
Objection!

00:03:31.961 --> 00:03:33.713
There's no need to change
the seating arrangements!

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:37.133
It's extremely filthy for guys and
girls to get any closer than this!

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:38.510
Changing the seating arrangements, huh?!

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:39.928
That sounds fun!

00:03:39.928 --> 00:03:42.013
I'm all for it!

00:03:42.013 --> 00:03:45.183
That sounds exciting! I'll definitely
take the seat next to Cayenne.

00:03:45.183 --> 00:03:48.019
--What?!
--Most are in favor, huh?

00:03:48.019 --> 00:03:51.940
Something's wrong with everyone!
They're impure... They're impure!

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.650
So how are we gonna decide?

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.443
It's gotta be drawing lots, right?

00:03:55.443 --> 00:04:00.073
Hey, hey! Then I'll draw for Shrade
and Cayenne, since they're absent!

00:04:14.629 --> 00:04:21.136
Okay! With this, my school life
will be holey... I mean, rosy...!

00:04:24.889 --> 00:04:26.975
I'm Malloy. Nice to meet you.

00:04:26.975 --> 00:04:29.310
Ah! You were in the battle sim, right?

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.730
I'm Ei Chang. Nice to meet you.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:32.897
Oh, is that right?

00:04:32.897 --> 00:04:34.399
Doesn't it sound fun?

00:04:34.399 --> 00:04:36.693
Why is this happening to me?

00:04:36.693 --> 00:04:37.694
Peek.

00:04:37.694 --> 00:04:40.030
Hm?

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:42.657
Of all people, the seat next to <i>him</i>?!

00:04:43.908 --> 00:04:45.410
Big bang...

00:04:48.038 --> 00:04:49.748
Huh?

00:04:49.748 --> 00:04:51.541
I'm glad I'm sitting next to you, Amata.

00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:53.126
S-Same here.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:55.086
I'm glad, too.

00:04:55.086 --> 00:04:57.672
It's kinda exciting, isn't it...?

00:04:57.672 --> 00:05:00.508
But not the same way battles are.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.262
Let me down!

00:05:04.262 --> 00:05:05.805
A-Amata...

00:05:09.434 --> 00:05:10.352
"Reserved" "Reserved"

00:05:10.352 --> 00:05:11.770
"Reserved" "Reserved"
Ahh...

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:15.231
To think that Cayenne and Shrade
will be sitting next to each other...

00:05:15.231 --> 00:05:18.276
This is definitely a miracle from God!

00:05:18.276 --> 00:05:21.529
Oh... I might go crazy!

00:05:23.365 --> 00:05:25.784
This is the first time for us to
sit next to each other, isn't it...?

00:05:25.784 --> 00:05:27.619
It'll be the first and the last time.

00:05:27.619 --> 00:05:30.789
I'm glad you came to
pick me up, my good friend.

00:05:30.789 --> 00:05:32.874
I didn't come to pick you up.

00:05:32.874 --> 00:05:35.126
It was just on my way to
go search for Abductors.

00:05:35.126 --> 00:05:37.087
--Look ahead.
--Whoa!

00:05:39.589 --> 00:05:43.343
Good grief... That was
an insensitive dissonance.

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:45.387
You jerk...!

00:05:45.387 --> 00:05:47.639
Just kidding, my good friend.

00:05:51.685 --> 00:05:57.065
Geez... everyone's warming up to each other.

00:05:57.065 --> 00:06:02.612
At any rate, who the heck
put a stuffed cat here?

00:06:02.612 --> 00:06:05.156
Stuffed animal...? I've got it!

00:06:06.116 --> 00:06:08.326
Ahhh! It's here!

00:06:08.326 --> 00:06:09.994
A horrifying stuffed animal!

00:06:09.994 --> 00:06:11.162
Huh?!

00:06:11.162 --> 00:06:12.372
What's going on?

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:14.624
What about a stuffed animal?

00:06:14.624 --> 00:06:16.209
Do you guys know...

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:19.587
...the rumor in Neo-DEAVA about
the Element who disappeared?

00:06:19.587 --> 00:06:21.381
Hm? What're you talking about?

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:24.467
It was a few years ago.

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:28.013
A girl transferred to this academy.

00:06:28.013 --> 00:06:33.977
But she was so shy that she
couldn't make any friends.

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:37.939
She couldn't bear the loneliness,

00:06:37.939 --> 00:06:43.028
and one day, she suddenly
disappeared from this academy.

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:47.907
Don't tell me...

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:49.826
She lost hope and...

00:06:50.827 --> 00:06:54.247
A stuffed animal was her only friend.

00:06:54.247 --> 00:07:00.628
Ever since, this stuffed animal can
be seen wandering about at night.

00:07:00.628 --> 00:07:03.131
As if trying to express the girl's sorrow,

00:07:03.131 --> 00:07:09.012
it sings with a beautiful and yet sad voice.

00:07:09.012 --> 00:07:11.139
How ridiculous!

00:07:11.139 --> 00:07:14.059
I've heard of that rumor, too.

00:07:14.059 --> 00:07:15.352
After the Berlin Wall collapsed,

00:07:15.352 --> 00:07:17.354
I heard that it's even started
appearing in the boys' dorm.

00:07:17.354 --> 00:07:19.522
If even Malloy says so...

00:07:19.522 --> 00:07:20.940
It really may be true.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:23.360
Oh, no, that's scary!

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:24.819
--Ahh!
--Ahh!

00:07:24.819 --> 00:07:26.905
The stuffed animal just moved!

00:07:26.905 --> 00:07:27.906
Andy...

00:07:27.906 --> 00:07:30.367
Enough of your fooling around!

00:07:30.367 --> 00:07:34.412
No, it's true! It really moved!

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:50.261
Mission complete.

00:07:50.261 --> 00:07:52.305
Just as we'd expect from you, Jin.

00:07:52.305 --> 00:07:53.556
Thanks.

00:07:53.556 --> 00:07:59.354
However, simulations exist
for actual battles, right?

00:07:59.354 --> 00:08:00.772
What's going on with Kagura?

00:08:00.772 --> 00:08:04.275
He'll probably be grounded
for a while this time.

00:08:04.275 --> 00:08:07.570
The invisible door... The door to the future...

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:10.407
It goes flying to the edge of the world.

00:08:13.243 --> 00:08:17.080
I'll take a peek on the other
side of the door again.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:21.668
I'm counting on you... Altair's last child...

00:08:33.805 --> 00:08:35.598
It's finally finished.

00:08:40.103 --> 00:08:42.605
Oh...? Um, Zessica?

00:08:42.605 --> 00:08:45.150
H-Hey! Were you on cleaning duty?

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.444
Yeah. I just finished, so I'm
heading back to my dorm now.

00:08:47.444 --> 00:08:50.321
I-I see! What a coincidence!

00:08:50.321 --> 00:08:52.365
I'm heading back now, too!

00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:55.160
--Yeah...?
--Say, do you wanna go back together?

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:57.704
--What?
--You don't have to be shy!

00:08:57.704 --> 00:08:59.706
I'll allow you to come back with me!

00:09:09.341 --> 00:09:11.092
Huh?

00:09:11.092 --> 00:09:13.511
No way... They don't open?

00:09:13.511 --> 00:09:15.680
Looks like we have no choice
but to leave from the back doors.

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:18.683
Well then, we're headed opposite
ways from here, so see ya.

00:09:18.683 --> 00:09:21.603
Ah! Hey, wait!

00:09:21.603 --> 00:09:23.104
Huh?

00:09:24.105 --> 00:09:26.191
Would you like to go back
via the exit on the girls' side?

00:09:26.191 --> 00:09:29.611
Huh...? That's fine, but why?

00:09:42.707 --> 00:09:44.709
Zessica?

00:09:44.709 --> 00:09:47.253
Well... it's hard to walk like that.

00:09:47.253 --> 00:09:50.048
S-Sorry!

00:09:50.048 --> 00:09:53.885
Um... could it be that you're... scared?

00:09:53.885 --> 00:09:57.138
D-Don't be ridiculous! Why would I be?!

00:09:57.138 --> 00:10:02.352
A-A story about walking stuffed animals
or a story about a singing ghost...

00:10:02.352 --> 00:10:04.354
Th-There's no way that I'd
take stuff like that seriously!

00:10:05.355 --> 00:10:06.856
What?!

00:10:09.734 --> 00:10:11.528
A-A stuffed animal...

00:10:11.528 --> 00:10:13.988
Wh-What's it doing in a place like this?

00:10:23.039 --> 00:10:26.209
Can't be...! That story was made up, right?

00:10:26.209 --> 00:10:29.129
I-I bet someone's playing a prank on us!

00:11:03.538 --> 00:11:05.915
You stink and taste sweet.

00:11:06.875 --> 00:11:08.793
I was scared...

00:11:08.793 --> 00:11:11.588
But is that the only reason why...

00:11:11.588 --> 00:11:14.924
...I can't forget about him?

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:19.304
Yeah, I wonder why...

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:24.017
Don't grab me there!

00:11:24.017 --> 00:11:28.480
No! Don't leave me!

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:32.567
Oh, no... Zessica and Amata are...

00:11:37.113 --> 00:11:38.615
Stop it, Jin!

00:11:38.615 --> 00:11:42.369
Leave my damn woman alone!

00:11:44.662 --> 00:11:51.336
Well... can you find clues... on the true Eve?

00:11:55.674 --> 00:11:57.759
I really saw it!

00:11:57.759 --> 00:11:59.552
The stuffed cat?

00:11:59.552 --> 00:12:02.222
That's right! It was walking
in the hallway at night!

00:12:02.222 --> 00:12:03.723
You saw it too, right, Amata?!

00:12:03.723 --> 00:12:05.058
I most definitely did!

00:12:05.058 --> 00:12:08.853
That's just a made-up story.
Don't take it seriously.

00:12:08.853 --> 00:12:10.855
You're the one who brought
it up in the first place!

00:12:10.855 --> 00:12:14.109
It was really walking!
We also heard it singing, too.

00:12:14.109 --> 00:12:18.655
Yeah, yeah. Going through puberty
can make you see things sometimes.

00:12:18.655 --> 00:12:20.532
You're our age, too!

00:12:20.532 --> 00:12:22.492
More importantly!

00:12:22.492 --> 00:12:26.162
What were you two doing
together that late at night?

00:12:26.162 --> 00:12:29.791
--What?
--Oh, that's because Zessica--

00:12:29.791 --> 00:12:30.875
Wh-What?

00:12:30.875 --> 00:12:34.504
Don't tell them I'm timid! It's embarrassing.

00:12:34.504 --> 00:12:35.755
Huh?

00:12:35.755 --> 00:12:37.298
What're you two whispering to each other?

00:12:37.298 --> 00:12:38.967
What? Well, um...

00:12:38.967 --> 00:12:42.721
So it's the sort of thing you
can't talk about?! How impure!

00:12:42.721 --> 00:12:45.432
The academy is sacred.
Don't tell me you two were--

00:12:45.432 --> 00:12:47.475
It's not what you're thinking!

00:12:47.475 --> 00:12:48.935
I saw it.

00:12:48.935 --> 00:12:52.188
You saw the stuffed animal
walking, too, Mikono?!

00:12:53.398 --> 00:12:54.858
What I saw was...

00:12:54.858 --> 00:12:58.570
...Zessica and Amata in each
other's arms in the courtyard!

00:12:58.570 --> 00:12:59.571
What?!

00:12:59.571 --> 00:13:02.615
And Zessica said, "Don't leave me!"

00:13:02.615 --> 00:13:03.742
What?!

00:13:03.742 --> 00:13:06.244
Is that what you call a lovers' quarrel?!

00:13:06.244 --> 00:13:07.746
Then you two really are...

00:13:07.746 --> 00:13:09.456
Y-You got it wrong!

00:13:09.456 --> 00:13:11.249
Mikono!

00:13:12.917 --> 00:13:15.128
An Abductor has appeared
in the Neo Kowloon area!

00:13:15.128 --> 00:13:15.337
"Class II Interception Positions"

00:13:15.337 --> 00:13:16.254
"Class II Interception Positions"
Elements are expected to

00:13:16.254 --> 00:13:18.631
take up Class II Interception Positions immediately!

00:13:18.631 --> 00:13:19.674
I repeat!

00:13:19.674 --> 00:13:23.345
Elements are expected to take up Class II
Interception Positions immediately!

00:13:28.391 --> 00:13:31.436
Analysis complete. Pattern B.

00:13:31.436 --> 00:13:34.147
It's progressing as it was in the simulation.

00:13:34.147 --> 00:13:37.108
The Abductor is moving forward
while destroying buildings in its way!

00:13:37.108 --> 00:13:39.277
Its speed is 60 per hour!

00:13:39.277 --> 00:13:43.656
This is strange. It doesn't seem like
its objective is abducting people.

00:13:43.656 --> 00:13:45.950
We can't allow the damage to increase.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:47.118
Zessica will be the head!

00:13:47.118 --> 00:13:50.330
--Roger!
--Cayenne and Amata! You two take off, too!

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:51.831
Roger!

00:13:59.297 --> 00:14:01.216
Mikono...

00:14:01.216 --> 00:14:03.385
She totally got the wrong idea.

00:14:03.385 --> 00:14:07.681
The firing accuracy and range of the
enemy's optical weapon are unknown.

00:14:07.681 --> 00:14:08.890
Be very careful!

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:10.392
Roger!

00:14:12.185 --> 00:14:13.186
A surprise attack?!

00:14:13.186 --> 00:14:14.729
Where is it firing from?!

00:14:14.729 --> 00:14:17.107
Firing error is 0.0003!

00:14:17.107 --> 00:14:18.191
Can't be!

00:14:18.191 --> 00:14:20.819
Optical weapons get directly
affected by the atmosphere.

00:14:20.819 --> 00:14:22.946
And yet, its fire is that accurate?!

00:14:22.946 --> 00:14:24.614
Radius Gnis...

00:14:24.614 --> 00:14:26.991
--What?
--Fudo...?

00:14:26.991 --> 00:14:30.161
It can even hone in on a coin 1,000 miles away

00:14:30.161 --> 00:14:35.000
and accurately pierce through it with
an unparalleled, perfect, cruel arrow!

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.127
H-How do you know that?

00:14:38.753 --> 00:14:40.422
You can tell by looking at it.

00:14:42.882 --> 00:14:46.803
Merge now! The Vector machines won't
be able to take a direct hit from that!

00:14:46.803 --> 00:14:49.639
Fly low and close in on him!

00:14:49.639 --> 00:14:53.393
Kinkyuu Gattai! Go! Aquarion!

00:14:59.357 --> 00:15:02.027
Aquarion Gepart!

00:15:07.407 --> 00:15:10.160
The evacuation of that area is already complete.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.245
I'll give you permission
to use buildings as shields!

00:15:12.245 --> 00:15:15.415
--Roger!
--Our attacks are still out of reach!

00:15:15.415 --> 00:15:19.085
We got just one machine as our enemy after all.
We'll follow its blind spots and get closer!

00:15:26.176 --> 00:15:28.386
You're moving as I expected.

00:15:28.386 --> 00:15:32.098
I want to make you experience
a desperate situation!

00:15:34.601 --> 00:15:37.187
The enemy shot out small flying objects!

00:15:37.187 --> 00:15:38.855
Missiles?!

00:15:38.855 --> 00:15:40.357
What are these?

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:48.573
What?!

00:15:50.241 --> 00:15:53.078
Dammit! If we don't do anything...

00:15:56.539 --> 00:16:00.043
The balls in the air reflect the laser!

00:16:00.043 --> 00:16:02.754
It seems that they make it possible
to attack from all directions!

00:16:02.754 --> 00:16:05.006
This is troublesome.

00:16:05.006 --> 00:16:07.676
No shields are effective.

00:16:13.973 --> 00:16:16.976
It's like we're fighting several machines!

00:16:16.976 --> 00:16:18.645
Zessica! Behind you!

00:16:23.441 --> 00:16:24.943
Amata!

00:16:28.446 --> 00:16:30.407
The laser is focused on Vector Z!

00:16:30.407 --> 00:16:32.784
Amata Sora's spirit level is dropping!

00:16:32.784 --> 00:16:33.827
Amata...

00:16:33.827 --> 00:16:36.454
It's getting to the limit!
The Gattai will be canceled!

00:16:42.293 --> 00:16:43.795
Amata!

00:16:43.795 --> 00:16:45.296
It's my fault!

00:16:45.296 --> 00:16:48.925
If I had been piloting
Aquarion more carefully...!

00:16:48.925 --> 00:16:50.719
Zessica's spirit level is dropping!

00:16:50.719 --> 00:16:53.638
50, 40, now below 30%!

00:16:53.638 --> 00:16:56.516
Amata was the one who received the damage!

00:16:56.516 --> 00:16:58.685
Zessica...

00:16:58.685 --> 00:17:02.188
A person's mind cannot be seen.

00:17:02.188 --> 00:17:06.234
Hence, misunderstandings
develop and create friction.

00:17:06.234 --> 00:17:09.112
However, Mikono Suzushiro...

00:17:09.112 --> 00:17:13.158
...know that some things are possible
precisely because of invisibility.

00:17:13.158 --> 00:17:14.826
What?

00:17:14.826 --> 00:17:18.246
Now is the time for us to turn
the invisible mind into power!

00:17:18.246 --> 00:17:20.498
Element Change!

00:17:20.498 --> 00:17:24.127
We'll replace Zessica Wong with Yunoha Suroor!

00:17:24.127 --> 00:17:25.879
--What?!
--Yunoha?

00:17:25.879 --> 00:17:27.297
Who's that?

00:17:27.297 --> 00:17:28.798
Huh?

00:17:38.808 --> 00:17:40.685
--Whoa!
--A stuffed animal?!

00:17:40.685 --> 00:17:42.729
Ah... Um, well...

00:17:42.729 --> 00:17:44.356
Nice to meet you.

00:17:44.356 --> 00:17:45.857
It talked?!

00:17:48.109 --> 00:17:51.112
Amata... and Zessica...

00:17:51.112 --> 00:17:54.324
I'm sorry for scaring you two yesterday.

00:17:54.324 --> 00:17:57.202
It caused Mikono to have
a terrible misunderstanding.

00:17:57.202 --> 00:17:59.704
--What?
--That's right! A misunderstanding!

00:17:59.704 --> 00:18:03.708
If you saw something like that walking
at night, you'd get panicked too, right?

00:18:03.708 --> 00:18:05.418
I'm really sorry.

00:18:05.418 --> 00:18:09.673
But for now, please trust me and fight with me.

00:18:09.673 --> 00:18:11.925
Are you... an Element, too?

00:18:13.593 --> 00:18:15.720
You can talk later, Amata!

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:20.517
Amata... I know I'm like this,
but could you merge with me?

00:18:20.517 --> 00:18:23.687
Okay, I'll trust you!

00:18:23.687 --> 00:18:28.733
Shinrei Gattai! Go! Aquarion!

00:18:41.121 --> 00:18:43.415
No...! They'll see me!

00:18:43.415 --> 00:18:46.584
They can see me!

00:18:46.584 --> 00:18:48.586
I can see! I can see!

00:18:48.586 --> 00:18:51.339
So that's how you really look!

00:18:52.841 --> 00:18:56.261
They see everything. I feel embarrassed!

00:18:56.261 --> 00:18:58.888
But I feel good.

00:19:00.056 --> 00:19:02.684
Aquarion Evol!

00:19:03.810 --> 00:19:06.604
Another form of the Mechanical Angel...

00:19:06.604 --> 00:19:08.773
I've already run simulations on that one, too.

00:19:10.775 --> 00:19:14.320
The transfer student who disappeared...
To think she really existed...

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:16.031
On top of that, she's cute!

00:19:16.031 --> 00:19:19.451
Oh, no! If you stare at me like that, I'll...

00:19:25.623 --> 00:19:27.584
--I missed?!
--What?!

00:19:27.584 --> 00:19:29.419
Aquarion disappeared?!

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:34.716
The laser passed through?!

00:19:34.716 --> 00:19:37.719
Her shy heart multiplies her power

00:19:37.719 --> 00:19:41.139
and makes things completely transparent.

00:19:41.139 --> 00:19:46.227
This is indeed Yunoha Suroor's Element power.

00:19:46.227 --> 00:19:51.149
It's a technique made possible by
the lovely, humble heart of a maiden.

00:19:51.149 --> 00:19:53.151
But please be careful.

00:19:53.151 --> 00:19:57.655
I can't make the entire Aquarion
transparent for very long.

00:19:57.655 --> 00:19:59.157
That's enough for us!

00:19:59.157 --> 00:20:00.617
This is incredible, Yunoha!

00:20:00.617 --> 00:20:03.036
I never imagined I'd be
complimented this much...

00:20:03.036 --> 00:20:05.705
I'm so... embarrassed.

00:20:10.669 --> 00:20:12.545
Both the lasers and sensors are useless?

00:20:12.545 --> 00:20:15.215
I didn't see this situation in the simulations!

00:20:22.514 --> 00:20:24.307
The distance to the enemy is 800!

00:20:24.307 --> 00:20:26.184
Close in on it like this!

00:20:26.184 --> 00:20:27.686
Okay!

00:20:30.647 --> 00:20:34.734
I see... It's simply that it cannot be seen.

00:20:34.734 --> 00:20:38.363
Even if it looks as if it disappeared,
it actually still exists there.

00:20:38.363 --> 00:20:40.699
Then, I'll use actual bullets and...

00:20:44.994 --> 00:20:46.496
Did I do it?!

00:20:58.174 --> 00:21:01.886
<i>I'm </i>experiencing... a desperate situation!

00:21:01.886 --> 00:21:05.265
--Now!
--An invisible fist brings down the enemy!

00:21:07.475 --> 00:21:11.062
Subliminal Punch!

00:21:16.317 --> 00:21:18.111
Okay! We did it!

00:21:20.071 --> 00:21:21.239
They won...

00:21:21.239 --> 00:21:23.116
Thanks to that ghost...?

00:21:34.085 --> 00:21:36.504
I guess I can't expect too much
from piloting in a different dimension

00:21:36.504 --> 00:21:38.882
via remote control.

00:21:38.882 --> 00:21:43.303
I got some data on the new Rare Igura.

00:21:43.303 --> 00:21:45.347
The power to be invisible, huh?

00:21:50.769 --> 00:21:51.895
Amata!

00:21:51.895 --> 00:21:53.271
Mikono!

00:21:53.271 --> 00:21:55.273
Zessica told me...

00:21:55.273 --> 00:21:57.776
So I jumped to the
wrong conclusion, didn't I...?

00:21:57.776 --> 00:21:58.860
I'm sorry!

00:21:58.860 --> 00:22:00.403
Don't worry about it.

00:22:02.655 --> 00:22:04.866
Oh... This is our new friend.

00:22:04.866 --> 00:22:07.452
Yes, I'm Yunoha.

00:22:07.452 --> 00:22:10.622
You're the ghost of an Element
who died a long time ago, right?

00:22:10.622 --> 00:22:11.706
What?

00:22:11.706 --> 00:22:14.751
But don't worry. We won't
be scared of you anymore.

00:22:14.751 --> 00:22:17.379
Let's work hard together as friends!

00:22:17.379 --> 00:22:18.755
Hey, hold on a sec.

00:22:18.755 --> 00:22:21.299
It's not like that, Amata. She is...

00:22:21.299 --> 00:22:24.928
Um... it seems that you have the wrong idea.

00:22:24.928 --> 00:22:29.432
I'm sorry... I'm alive.

00:22:29.432 --> 00:22:31.768
--What?
--Her name is Yunoha Suroor.

00:22:31.768 --> 00:22:34.979
She's an Element candidate just like you guys.

00:22:36.398 --> 00:22:38.149
Sorry!

00:22:38.149 --> 00:22:40.318
I'm floating!

00:22:40.318 --> 00:22:42.696
Let me down!

00:22:42.696 --> 00:22:44.989
So I guess Amata floats...

00:22:44.989 --> 00:22:47.492
...with pretty much anyone, huh?

00:22:56.167 --> 00:23:01.631
<i>Kaze ni ubawareta wake janai</i>

00:23:01.631 --> 00:23:04.509
<i>Katamichi bun no yuuki de</i>

00:23:04.509 --> 00:23:12.308
<i>Bokura higeki o ukeireru</i>

00:23:12.308 --> 00:23:17.022
<i>Kokoro ga koko ni atta hazu no kuudou</i>

00:23:17.022 --> 00:23:19.607
<i>Motto boku ga ookikereba</i>

00:23:19.607 --> 00:23:25.280
<i>Kimi o mirai o sukueta darou ka</i>

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:32.579
<i>Taisetsu na hito o mamoru sube o</i>
<i>tatta hitotsu shika motanai</i>

00:23:32.579 --> 00:23:39.419
<i>Sonna anata ga hagure tadayou sora</i>

00:23:39.419 --> 00:23:47.135
<i>Anata ijou no hito ni deaenai</i>

00:23:47.135 --> 00:23:53.600
<i>Tsuki ni aragau nagai furea</i>

00:23:53.600 --> 00:24:00.148
<i>Hajimari mo sezu owaru monogatari</i>

00:24:00.148 --> 00:24:06.112
<i>Kizutsukiuru yawarakasa tojikometa senritsu</i>

00:24:06.112 --> 00:24:09.157
<i>Kanaderu hodo utau hodo</i>

00:24:09.157 --> 00:24:14.621
<i>Kowareru hodo ni</i>

00:24:14.621 --> 00:24:21.544
<i>Anataga koishii</i>

00:24:23.672 --> 00:24:25.757
My name is Zessica Wong.

00:24:25.757 --> 00:24:28.885
I'm 17. People often say that
I dress with too much exposure.

00:24:28.885 --> 00:24:30.929
My cleavage is openly shown,

00:24:30.929 --> 00:24:34.265
but what's inside my heart
is a secret to everyone.

00:24:34.432 --> 00:24:36.101
"Next Episode 'Expose'"
Next on <i>Aquarion Evol</i>!

00:24:36.101 --> 00:24:37.227
"Next Episode 'Expose'"
"Expose."
